    "acceptance-fire-patterns": {
      "_why": [
        "R6 by firing episodes (design 7.14). An episode is a run of consecutive firing rows",
        "closed by a clear (v1 severity clear, v2 status resolved); firing rows after the last",
        "clear are the open episode, and open_since is its first row's time when the LAST row",
        "is firing. flapping: >= 3 cycles in a rolling 24h, any provider. spamming: API only,",
        "n x 24h >= 24 x span and span >= 6h (span = last - first). Grafana writes a row per",
        "evaluation, so repeated Grafana rows are never spamming. stuck: Grafana whose last",
        "row is firing with (last firing row - open_since) >= 72h, inclusive. Never measured",
        "to window_end: Grafana writes a row per evaluation while firing, so silence after",
        "the last row means it stopped firing; one row spans 0h and is never stuck.",
        "Priority flapping -> spamming -> stuck. max_episode_firing_rows is a diagnostic.",
        "(a) F every 12h from 08-21 12:00 to 08-24 12:00 (7 rows), no clear: rows span",
        "exactly 72h => stuck (inclusive). 1 row 08-21, 2 each on 08-22, 08-23, 08-24.",
        "(b) F every 12h from 08-21 12:01 to 08-24 00:01 (6 rows) + F 08-24 12:00, no clear:",
        "rows span 71h59m => none. 1 row 08-21, 2 each on 08-22, 08-23, 08-24.",
        "(c) F 01:00, F 01:05, C 01:10 on 08-24: closed => none.",
        "(d) F, F, F, C on 08-24 02:00-02:15: closed, Grafana => none (max episode 3).",
        "(e) F, C, F, F, C on 08-24 03:00-03:20: 2 cycles, closed => none.",
        "(f) F every 12h from 08-21 00:00 to 08-24 12:00 (8 rows), no clear: rows span 84h",
        "=> stuck. 2 rows on each of 08-21..08-24.",
        "(g) F/C pairs on 08-24, clears 00:05, 10:05, 20:05 => 3 cycles in 24h => flapping.",
        "(h) API, F F F C x3 on 08-23 (every 30 min, clears 01:30, 04:30, 08:00): 3 cycles",
        "=> flapping, which wins over spamming (12 rows over 8h: 12 x 24h >= 24 x 8h).",
        "(i) F/C pairs with clears 08-22 18:05, 08-23 07:05, 08-23 20:05 (26h first to last)",
        "=> at most 2 cycles in any [t, t+24h), ends on a clear => none. 2 rows 08-22, 4 08-23.",
        "(j) API, hourly 08-22 00:00..22:00 + 08-23 00:00 = 24 rows, span 24h => 24 x 24h >=",
        "24 x 24h => spamming. 23 rows on 08-22, 1 on 08-23.",
        "(k) API, hourly 08-22 00:00..21:00 + 08-23 00:00 = 23 rows, span 24h => none.",
        "(l) API, 30 rows 10 min apart from 08-24 00:00: span 4h50m < 6h => none.",
        "(m) API, 5 rows 25h apart from 08-20 00:00, no clear, span 100h: 5 x 24h < 24 x",
        "100h and stuck is Grafana-only => none. One row per date 08-20..08-24.",
        "(p) ONE Grafana F at 08-21 14:00 (100h before window_end), then silence: one row",
        "spans 0h => none. Measured to window_end it would be stuck (final review C1).",
        "v1 rows by date: 08-20 1 (m); 08-21 6 (a, b, f 2, m, p); 08-22 54 (a 2, b 2, f 2,",
        "i 2, j 23, k 22, m); 08-23 25 (a 2, b 2, f 2, h 12, i 4, j, k, m); 08-24 55 (a 2,",
        "b 2, f 2, c 3, d 4, e 5, g 6, l 30, m). 141.",
        "v1 distinct by date: 1, 5, 7, 8, 9 => 30/7.",
        "R6 on every row of a, f, g, h, j: 08-21 [3,2] (a, f 2); 08-22 [27,3] (a 2, f 2,",
        "j 23); 08-23 [17,4] (a 2, f 2, h 12, j); 08-24 [10,3] (a 2, f 2, g 6). 57 rows;",
        "distinct sum 12.",
        "Model: b, c, d, e, i, k, l, m, p (9) are assessed_good, counted once on every date",
        "they appear: 08-20 m; 08-21 b, m, p; 08-22 b, i, k, m; 08-23 b, i, k, m; 08-24 b, c,",
        "d, e, l, m => 1 + 3 + 4 + 4 + 6 = 18.",
        "Batches: b, c, d, e, i, p share the v1 rule URL (6); k, l, m are API with no URL =>",
        "one application group of 3.",
        "v2 (n) flapping: F 08-21 12:00, then R 02:00, F 06:00, R 08:00, F 12:00, R 14:00 on",
        "08-23 => 3 clears in 12h; ends resolved. (o) stuck: one row per 12h evaluation from",
        "08-21 00:00 to 08-25 12:00 (10 rows), never resolved: rows span 108h.",
        "v2 rows by date: 08-21 3 (n, o 2); 08-22 2; 08-23 7 (n 5, o 2); 08-24 2; 08-25 2 =",
        "16. Distinct 2, 1, 2, 1, 1 => 7/7. Both R6 on every row. Both ready => 100%.",
        "One node_name per object, so node and key operands equal distinct per date.",
        "No panels, so unseen is NULL on both schemas. Both schemas present => phase_1."
      ],
